      "css": ".ds-banner{font-family:'Public Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;border-radius:6px;padding:12px 16px;border:1px solid #E8CFA8;background:#FBF3E8;color:#2E3F3C;font-size:0.93rem;line-height:1.55}.ds-banner svg{color:#9A5B16;flex:none;margin-top:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Inflation Report",
    "overview": "FinSight reads as a central bank's quarterly report on its own models. The page is a white report ground framed by a deep-teal shell; results are set as numbered exhibits, each followed by a source line, and every estimate that has a spread is drawn with its uncertainty band. Structure comes from hairline rules, not from boxes or shadows: a thick teal rule opens a page, an ink rule opens a table of figures, a pale rule opens each section.\n\nDensity is that of a publication, not a dashboard: one workhorse sans with tabular figures, a reading measure held under 75ch for standfirsts and captions, and colour reserved for meaning (teal for the house, the three sentiment hues for verdicts, ochre for the one thing that needs attention). The world refuses the dark, glowing KPI-card dashboard: no gradient fills, no card shadows, no glow.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White report ground, cool mist panels, deep-teal sidebar shell.",
      "Hairline rules carry all structure; shadows are absent at rest.",
      "Numbered exhibits with a \"Source:\" line beneath.",
      "Uncertainty drawn as bands: dot-and-interval charts, segmented probability bands.",
      "Sentiment always triple-coded: colour, glyph (▲ ▶ ▼) and word.",
      "One sans (Public Sans, self-hosted 400/500/600/700), tabular lining figures wherever numbers appear.",
      "Sentence case for every heading, label and action in the report body."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Colour Rule",
        "body": "Outside the shell and the house teal, colour encodes a class or a state. A key figure takes a sentiment colour only when its value is that sentiment; otherwise it is ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Triple-Code Rule",
        "body": "Sentiment is never colour alone: positive is green ▲, neutral is slate ▶, negative is oxblood ▼, and the word is always written beside the glyph.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every number on screen (figures, metrics, dataframes, tables, band legends) uses `tabular-nums lining-nums`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Headings, labels, buttons and table heads in the report body are sentence case. The only uppercase, tracked text in the system is the sidebar's navigation group labels (0.7-0.72rem, 700, 0.12em), which belong to the shell, not the report.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Structure is drawn with 1px rules (3px for the masthead). If a container needs separating, give it a rule or a mist fill, never a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open every page with the masthead and number its results as exhibits, each followed by a \"Source:\" line naming the results file.",
      "**Do** draw any estimate with a spread as a band (interval chart or probability band) rather than a bare number.",
      "**Do** pair every sentiment colour with its glyph (▲ positive, ▶ neutral, ▼ negative) and its word.",
      "**Do** set key figures as one ruled row with an ink top rule and hairline dividers.",
      "**Do** use tabular lining figures for every number and keep every text colour at 4.5:1 or better.",
      "**Do** use Material Symbols for native widgets and the authored 1.75-stroke SVG set inside custom HTML.",
      "**Do** take chart colours from the template sequence and sentiment hues from the sentiment tokens, never ad hoc hexes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put shadows, gradients or glows on containers; separate with hairlines or a mist fill.",
      "**Don't** return to the dark, glowing KPI-card dashboard or rounded metric cards.",
      "**Don't** encode sentiment by colour alone, or colour a figure that is not a sentiment value.",
      "**Don't** add eyebrows or kickers above headings, gradient text, or emoji icons.",
      "**Don't** use title case or uppercase in the report body; uppercase tracking belongs to the shell's nav group labels only.",
      "**Don't** load a second typeface; Public Sans carries every role."
    ]
  }
}